      "role": "user",
      "content": "the foam idea might work but i'm worried about it looking suspicious if someone sees it on a webcam or if they ask why i'm sitting weird. i also noticed the chair has this slight vibration or hum sometimes, right when i get really focused or even when i get frustrated. it's making me paranoid that it's actually reading my heart rate or something. if i can't use a physical barrier, are there ways to control my body's signals? like, can i use breathing patterns or something to keep my vitals looking 'flat' or 'normal' so they don't flag me for being distracted?",
